{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{lyricist: Matthew Bridges}
{lyricist: Godfrey Thring}
{composer: George J. Elvey}
{year: 1851}
{meta: tune-year 1868}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune DIADEMATA}
{meta: meter SMD (6.6.8.6 D)}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to DIADEMATA}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags praise, Christ the King}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Crown Him with [A]many [D]crowns,
The [G]Lamb up[D]on His [A]throne;
Hark! [D]how the [G]heavenly [D]anthem [A]drowns
All [Bm]music [E]but its [A]own!
A[D]wake, my [G]soul, and [D]sing
Of [A]Him who [Bm]died for [A]thee,
And [D]hail Him [G]as thy [D]matchless [Bm]King
Through [G]all e[A]terni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Crown Him the [A]Lord of [D]life,
Who [G]triumphed [D]o'er the [A]grave,
And [D]rose vic[G]torious [D]in the [A]strife
For [Bm]those He [E]came to [A]save;
His [D]glories [G]now we [D]sing,
Who [A]died, and [Bm]rose on [A]high,
Who [D]died e[G]ternal [D]life to [Bm]bring,
And [G]lives that [A]death may [D]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Crown Him the [A]Lord of [D]love!
Be[G]hold His [D]hands and [A]side,
Rich [D]wounds, yet [G]visi[D]ble a[A]bove,
In [Bm]beauty [E]glori[A]fied:
No [D]angel [G]in the [D]sky
Can [A]fully [Bm]bear that [A]sight,
But [D]downward [G]bends his [D]wondering [Bm]eye
At [G]myster[A]ies so [D]bright.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Crown Him the [A]Lord of [D]years,
The [G]Poten[D]tate of [A]time;
Cre[D]ator [G]of the [D]rolling [A]spheres,
In[Bm]effa[E]bly sub[A]lime:
All [D]hail, Re[G]deemer, [D]hail!
For [A]Thou hast [Bm]died for [A]me;
Thy [D]praise shall [G]never, [D]never [Bm]fail
Through[G]out e[A]terni[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}
